        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25422372</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>ZFA:0009143</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>All brush border cells are columnar-cuboidal.  The formal logical definition of this term asserts this. Brush border epithelial cells are predominantly found lining the small intestine and the proximal tubules of the kidneys.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>brush border epithelial cell</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
