    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00007089 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00007089">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00007003"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The outermost cellular layer of the nervous system, probably of mesodermal origin (Hartenstein and Jan, 1992). This layer consists of glial cells, which participate in nutrient uptake and establish a first diffusion barrier (Limmer et al., 2014).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>VFB:FBbt_00007089</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>apical glial cell</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>perineural sheath</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>perineurial sheath</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>fly_anatomy.ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>neural lamella</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>FBbt:00007089</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>Evidence of mesodermal origin comes from the observation that embryos lacking mesoderm lack this cell layer and the overlying neural lamella (Edwards et al., 1993).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>perineurial glial sheath</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00007089"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The outermost cellular layer of the nervous system, probably of mesodermal origin (Hartenstein and Jan, 1992). This layer consists of glial cells, which participate in nutrient uptake and establish a first diffusion barrier (Limmer et al., 2014).</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FlyBase:FBrf0057603</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FlyBase:FBrf0058936</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FlyBase:FBrf0226917</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00007089"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>apical glial cell</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FlyBase:FBrf0206543</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00007089"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>neural lamella</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FlyBase:FBrf0214261</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00007108 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00007108">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000075"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000255"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00058239"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000939"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A columnar epithelial cell with distinct apical-basal polarity. The apical surface has microvilli with dense plaques at their tips. A cortical network (ring) of actin filaments underlies the apical surface, extends into the microvilli and is associated with a zonula adherens which encircles each cell. Below this is a broad region of pleated sheet type septate junctions connecting all lateral surfaces to adjacent cells. Plaque-like gap junctions occur mainly interspersed among septate junctions and, at a lower frequency, below them. Small, sparsely distributed hemidesmosomes attach these cells to the underlying basal lamina.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000589>imaginal disc cell (drosophila)</obo:IAO_0000589>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>CL:0000429</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>fly_anatomy.ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>FBbt:00007108</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>imaginal disc epithelial cell</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00007108"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A columnar epithelial cell with distinct apical-basal polarity. The apical surface has microvilli with dense plaques at their tips. A cortical network (ring) of actin filaments underlies the apical surface, extends into the microvilli and is associated with a zonula adherens which encircles each cell. Below this is a broad region of pleated sheet type septate junctions connecting all lateral surfaces to adjacent cells. Plaque-like gap junctions occur mainly interspersed among septate junctions and, at a lower frequency, below them. Small, sparsely distributed hemidesmosomes attach these cells to the underlying basal lamina.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FlyBase:FBrf0064790</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00007137 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00007137">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000002"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00004875"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00048491"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cyst of female germ cells interconnected by ring canals. Each cyst originates from a single cystoblast which divides to form 16 cyst cells. These become enveloped in a follicle cell epithelium as they pass through region 2 of the germarium. Cysts that have left the germarium are termed egg chambers.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>fly_anatomy.ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>FBbt:00007137</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>female germline cyst</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00007137"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A cyst of female germ cells interconnected by ring canals. Each cyst originates from a single cystoblast which divides to form 16 cyst cells. These become enveloped in a follicle cell epithelium as they pass through region 2 of the germarium. Cysts that have left the germarium are termed egg chambers.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FlyBase:FBrf0064777</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00007141 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00007141">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00007003"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00048490"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cone shaped cluster of densely packed cells at the center of the germinal proliferation center. It is anchored to the tip of the testis via apical connections to the thick, convoluted basal lamina found there.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>fly_anatomy.ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>FBbt:00007141</oboInOwl:id>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/fbbt#FlyTed"/>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/fbbt#cur"/>
        <rdfs:label>germinal proliferation center hub</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00007141"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A cone shaped cluster of densely packed cells at the center of the germinal proliferation center. It is anchored to the tip of the testis via apical connections to the thick, convoluted basal lamina found there.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FlyBase:FBrf0064778</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


