    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00058247 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00058247">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00058244"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00058246"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Any adult neuron (FBbt:00047095) that is capable of some detection of pheromone (GO:0043695).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <terms:contributor rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6095-8718"/>
        <terms:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-09-27T15:58:18Z</terms:date>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>VFB:FBbt_00058247</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>fly_anatomy.ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>FBbt:00058247</oboInOwl:id>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/fbbt#cur"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Likely to be the ppk23 cells, as null mutants lose leg and proboscis responses to pheromones, however, function of ppk23 in wing margin was not investigated. (Thistle et al., 2012 - FBrf0218411). ppk23 cells are distinct from sugar and water cells, but a few cells coexpress Gr66a and ppk23 (Thistle et al., 2012). Some ppk23 cells also express ppk29, but not clear from Thistle et al. (2012) whether this is all or a subset.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>adult pheromone-sensing neuron</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
