    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00100044 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00100044">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00005927"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A gustatory receptor neuron that is responsive to high concentrations of salt or to bitter compounds, or both (Meunier et al., 2003; Montell, 2009). It triggers an aversive behavior (Freeman and Dahanukar, 2015).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <terms:contributor rdf:resource="https://www.researchgate.net/scientific-contributions/Simon-Reeve-2162827703"/>
        <terms:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2010-03-09T11:37:02Z</terms:date>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>L2 GRN</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>bitter neuron</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>VFB:FBbt_00100044</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>fly_anatomy.ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>FBbt:00100044</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>The projection of L2 GRNs (bitter-sensitive) of the labellum to the subesophageal zone, and of leg gustatory sensilla to the central brain are segregated from the projections of S cells (sugar-sensitive) to the thoracic ganglion (Wang et al., 2004).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>high salt/bitter-sensing neuron</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00100044"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A gustatory receptor neuron that is responsive to high concentrations of salt or to bitter compounds, or both (Meunier et al., 2003; Montell, 2009). It triggers an aversive behavior (Freeman and Dahanukar, 2015).</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FlyBase:FBrf0160792</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FlyBase:FBrf0208984</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
