            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A membranous fold of the heart that prevents reflux of fluid.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:RO_0002175 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_9606"/>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000001>One of the four structures within the heart that prevent backflow of blood by opening and closing with each heartbeat. The valves include two semilunar valves, the aortic and pulmonary; the mitral or bicuspid valve; and the tricuspid valve. The valves permit blood flow in only one direction. [TFD][VHOG]</obo:UBPROP_0000001>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000003>Extensive conservation of valve developmental mechanisms also has been observed among vertebrate species including chicken, mouse, and human.[well established][VHOG]</obo:UBPROP_0000003>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000013>Rector et al: One might be tempted to define &apos;heart valve&apos; equivalently to &apos;valve in the heart&apos;, and &apos;valve&apos; as a &apos;structure which functions as a valve&apos;. But this combination results in the &apos;foramen ovale&apos; being classified as a kind of &apos;heart valve&apos;, since it is undoubtedly located in the heart and functions as a valve</obo:UBPROP_0000013>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>BTO:0000564</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>EMAPA:17869</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
