        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBPROP_0000013"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The term leg can mean: [1] an appendage on which an animal walks [2] the entire hindlimb of a tetrapod [3] the segment of a human leg between knee and ankle (cf FMA) [4] the region of a hindlimb include the stylopod and zeugopod, but excluding the autopod. We define this class as [4], and thus &apos;leg&apos; is compltely analagous to &apos;arm&apos;. For [1], see the class &apos;locomotive weight-bearing appendage&apos;. For [2] we use &apos;hindlimb&apos;. For</owl:annotatedTarget>
