    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001160 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001160">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0009870"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The fundus is the portion of the stomach that lies above the cardiac notch, and contains the fundic glands[GO, Kardong].</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000001>The greater curvature of the stomach. [Dorian_AF, Elsevier&apos;s_encyclopaedic_dictionary_of_medicine, Part_B:_Anatomy_(1988)_Amsterdam_etc.:_Elsevier][VHOG]</obo:UBPROP_0000001>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000003>Although all vertebrates have a digestive tract and accessory glands, various parts of this system are not necessarily homologous, analogous, or even present in all species. Therefore, broad comparisons can be best made under the listings of headgut, foregut, midgut, pancreas and biliary system, hindgut.[uncertain][VHOG]</obo:UBPROP_0000003>
