        <obo:IAO_0000115>The most superficial muscle of the triceps surae group, in the posterior portion of the lower hindleg.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:RO_0002175 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_9606"/>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000001>The most superficial calf muscle in the posterior part of the leg. [TFD][VHOG]</obo:UBPROP_0000001>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000003>The most prominent ventral muscle of the shank is the gastrocnemius, the &apos;calf&apos; muscle. In mammals, it has two heads, resulting from the fusion of two different phylogenetic predecessors.[well established][VHOG]</obo:UBPROP_0000003>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000008>In mammals this muscle has two heads[ISBN:0073040584]</obo:UBPROP_0000008>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000009>involved in standing, walking, running and jumping</obo:UBPROP_0000009>
