        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0035612"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The small curved bones that extends horizontally along the lateral wall of the nasal passage.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:RO_0002161 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_436486"/>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000008>In humans, the turbinates divide the nasal airway into three groove-like air passages -and are responsible for forcing inhaled air to flow in a steady, regular pattern around the largest possible surface of cilia and climate controlling tissue.</obo:UBPROP_0000008>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000008>Turbinals are only ossified in birds and derived synapsids.</obo:UBPROP_0000008>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000012>FMA considers nasal concha and nasal concha of ethmoid bone to be synonymous. We disambiguate these here</obo:UBPROP_0000012>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>EHDAA2:0004101</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>EMAPA:25093</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>GAID:224</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>MA:0000286</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>MESH:D014420</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
