        <obo:IAO_0000115>Part of the hippocampal formation forming a &apos;V&apos; or &apos;U&apos; shaped structure with the opening bounded by hippocampal area CA3. It consists of 3 layers from superficial to deep: molecular, granule cell and polymorphic or hilar layer.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:RO_0002171 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001954"/>
        <obo:RO_0002171 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002601"/>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000001>The dentate gyrus is one of two interlocking gyri of the hippocampus. It contains granule cells, which project to the pyramidal cells and interneurons of the CA3 region of the ammon gyrus[GO][GO:0021542].</obo:UBPROP_0000001>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>BAMS:DG</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
