            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Crescent shaped outer zone of the nucleus accumbens, defined by a combination of chemoarchitecture and afferent and efferent connections. The shell is distinguished from the more centrally located core through the notable reduction in staining for the calcium-binding protein calbindin D28K, which is dense in the core and virtually absent in the shell.</obo:IAO_0000115>
